variable {d : ℕ}

/-! ## The scale step

The paper picks an even integer `Δ` larger than `max(δ, R₀)` and divisible by the
number `L` of reference cones, so that every town
`T_n = T(Δⁿ, Δⁿ⁻¹)` is `ϑ`-sparsely populated. -/

theorem QFS.sparselyPopulated_of_scaleStep {ϑ R₀ : ℝ} {L : ℕ} (Δ : ScaleStep d ϑ R₀ L)
    (hΔ0 : 0 < (Δ.val : ℝ)) (n : ℕ) :
    SparselyPopulated d ϑ ((Δ.val : ℝ) ^ (n + 1)) ((Δ.val : ℝ) ^ n) := by sorry
